      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e what is the project, and why aren\u0027t they using a supported build system?\nA virtual GPU driver project that plans to eventually merge into mesa - and that\u0027s the precise reason why we can\u0027t use neither Android.bp nor CMake. The upstream mesa uses the meson build system.\n\n\u003e bug?\nhttp://b/192614792 and http://b/175527587\n\n\u003e design doc?\nhttp://doc/1Bp4igeC8Yxr8V-XFubhT1XKYTb0TIvOuQJuFdl59tVw\n\n\u003e how many other external projects do you need to use?\nCurrently, we have the following external projects in use:\n* gfxstream-protocols(https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/gfxstream-protocols/)\n* Vulkan-headers(https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/vulkan-headers/, plan to retire)\n* angle(https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/angle/)\n* flatbuffers(this repo)\n* crosvm(https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/crosvm/)\n\n\u003e where does _your_ code live?\nVarious places including:\n* external/qemu on the emu-master-dev branch\n* device/generic/goldfish-opengl\n* device/generic/vulkan-cereal\n\nI am wondering if you know any guidelines I should follow to make a change to an external project in aosp on the master branch. Thanks!",
